@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-general-provisions`

-- Tests of usca-general-provisions.l4.  Each expected value is decided from the section cited above the assertion.  A failing assertion is a finding.

§ `Gov. Code § 14: shall is mandatory, may is permissive`

#ASSERT `the force of the word in the Government Code` shall EQUALS mandatory
#ASSERT `the force of the word in the Government Code` may EQUALS permissive

§ `Gov. Code § 7: a deputy or a person authorized pursuant to law may exercise a power of a public officer`

#ASSERT `a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `the officer` `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT `a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `a deputy of the officer` `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT `a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `a person the officer authorized pursuant to law` `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `a deputy of the officer` `given that` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `a person the officer authorized pursuant to law` `given that` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `the officer` `given that` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `a person the officer authorized, not pursuant to law` `given that` FALSE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 7 lets a deputy or a person authorized pursuant to law exercise the power; it does not say whether a person the officer authorized otherwise than pursuant to law may"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a power of a public officer may be exercised, or a duty performed, by` `another person` `given that` FALSE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 7 lets a deputy or a person authorized pursuant to law exercise the power; it does not say that no one else may"

§ `Civ. Code § 12, Code Civ. Proc. § 15: a joint authority of three or more is exercised by a majority`

#ASSERT `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 3 2 `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 3 1 `given that` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 3 3 `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 3 0 `given that` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 4 2 `given that` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 4 3 `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 5 3 `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 5 2 `given that` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 7 4 `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 7 3 `given that` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 2 2 `given that` FALSE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 12 and Code Civ. Proc. § 15 speak of a joint authority given to three or more officers or persons"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 1 1 `given that` FALSE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 12 and Code Civ. Proc. § 15 speak of a joint authority given to three or more officers or persons"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 3 2 `given that` TRUE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 12 and Code Civ. Proc. § 15 yield to what the Act giving the authority expresses; the Act decides"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 3 4 `given that` FALSE BECAUSE "the number acting cannot be negative or exceed the number holding the authority"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a joint authority may be exercised by those acting` 3 -1 `given that` FALSE BECAUSE "the number acting cannot be negative or exceed the number holding the authority"

§ `Gov. Code § 8: writing, and notices in English`

#ASSERT `a message is a writing` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a message is a writing` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a message is a writing` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a message is a writing` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 8 yields to what is expressly provided otherwise; the provision that does so decides the form"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 8 yields to what is expressly provided otherwise; the provision that does so decides the form"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 8 yields to what is expressly provided otherwise; the provision that does so decides the form"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a notice, report, statement or record required or authorized by the Government Code is made as the code requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 8 yields to what is expressly provided otherwise; the provision that does so decides the form"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the version of a document in two languages that has authority` BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 8 requires a notice, report, statement or record to be in English; no deposited section says which of two language versions of a document has authority"

§ `Gov. Code § 16, Civ. Code § 14(a), Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(11): signature by mark`

#ASSERT `a mark is a signature or subscription` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a mark is a signature or subscription` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a mark is a signature or subscription` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a mark is a signature or subscription` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a mark is a signature or subscription` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `a signature by mark can be acknowledged or serve as the signature to a sworn statement` TRUE 2
#ASSERT `a signature by mark can be acknowledged or serve as the signature to a sworn statement` TRUE 3
#ASSERT NOT (`a signature by mark can be acknowledged or serve as the signature to a sworn statement` TRUE 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`a signature by mark can be acknowledged or serve as the signature to a sworn statement` TRUE 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`a signature by mark can be acknowledged or serve as the signature to a sworn statement` FALSE 2)

§ `Gov. Code § 16.5: digital signature`

#ASSERT `a digital signature has the same force and effect as a manual signature` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature has the same force and effect as a manual signature` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature has the same force and effect as a manual signature` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature has the same force and effect as a manual signature` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature has the same force and effect as a manual signature` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature has the same force and effect as a manual signature` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a digital signature has the same force and effect as a manual signature` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a public entity is required to use or permit the use of a digital signature`)
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 16.5 applies to the digital signature` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 16.5 applies to the digital signature` TRUE)

§ `Code Civ. Proc. § 17(b)(3), § 34: electronic signature of a court or judicial officer`

#ASSERT `a thing is an electronic signature` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is an electronic signature` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is an electronic signature` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing is an electronic signature` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `an electronic signature is as effective as an original signature under Code Civ. Proc. § 34` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an electronic signature is as effective as an original signature under Code Civ. Proc. § 34` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `an electronic signature is as effective as an original signature under Code Civ. Proc. § 34` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 34 makes an electronic signature by a court or judicial officer as effective as an original signature; it does not say the same of anyone else's"
#ASSERT REFUSED `an electronic signature is as effective as an original signature under Code Civ. Proc. § 34` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 34 makes an electronic signature by a court or judicial officer as effective as an original signature; it does not say the same of anyone else's"

§ `Civ. Code § 17, Code Civ. Proc. § 11: certified mail where registered mail is required`

#ASSERT `a requirement of the Civil Code or the Code of Civil Procedure that a notice be mailed by registered mail is met by` `registered mail`
#ASSERT `a requirement of the Civil Code or the Code of Civil Procedure that a notice be mailed by registered mail is met by` `certified mail`
#ASSERT REFUSED `a requirement of the Civil Code or the Code of Civil Procedure that a notice be mailed by registered mail is met by` `another method of mailing` BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 17 and Code Civ. Proc. § 11 say that certified mail is a sufficient compliance where registered mail is required; no deposited section says whether any other method is"

§ `Deemed service and deemed notice: the deposit has no general rule`

-- No deposited section deems service made, or a notice given, on any day after it is sent.  The two functions refuse for every date, which is the answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day service by mail is deemed made, the document having been mailed on` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems service by mail made on any day: Civ. Code § 17 and Code Civ. Proc. § 11 say only that certified mail is sufficient where registered mail is required, and Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(b) counts method-of-service days backward from a hearing"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a notice is deemed given, the notice having been sent on` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems a notice given on any day after it is sent: Civ. Code §§ 18 and 19 define actual and constructive notice, and say nothing of the day a notice sent is given"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day service by mail is deemed made, the document having been mailed on` (YMD 2026 12 31) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems service by mail made on any day: Civ. Code § 17 and Code Civ. Proc. § 11 say only that certified mail is sufficient where registered mail is required, and Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(b) counts method-of-service days backward from a hearing"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a notice is deemed given, the notice having been sent on` (YMD 2026 12 31) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems a notice given on any day after it is sent: Civ. Code §§ 18 and 19 define actual and constructive notice, and say nothing of the day a notice sent is given"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day service by mail is deemed made, the document having been mailed on` (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems service by mail made on any day: Civ. Code § 17 and Code Civ. Proc. § 11 say only that certified mail is sufficient where registered mail is required, and Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(b) counts method-of-service days backward from a hearing"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a notice is deemed given, the notice having been sent on` (YMD 2024 2 29) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems a notice given on any day after it is sent: Civ. Code §§ 18 and 19 define actual and constructive notice, and say nothing of the day a notice sent is given"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day service by mail is deemed made, the document having been mailed on` (YMD 2026 2 28) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems service by mail made on any day: Civ. Code § 17 and Code Civ. Proc. § 11 say only that certified mail is sufficient where registered mail is required, and Code Civ. Proc. § 12c(b) counts method-of-service days backward from a hearing"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a notice is deemed given, the notice having been sent on` (YMD 2026 2 28) BECAUSE "no deposited section deems a notice given on any day after it is sent: Civ. Code §§ 18 and 19 define actual and constructive notice, and say nothing of the day a notice sent is given"

§ `Civ. Code § 18, § 19: notice`

#ASSERT `a person has actual notice of a fact` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person has actual notice of a fact` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a person has constructive notice of a fact` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person has constructive notice of a fact` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a person has constructive notice of the fact itself under Civ. Code § 19` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a person has constructive notice of the fact itself under Civ. Code § 19` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person has constructive notice of the fact itself under Civ. Code § 19` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person has constructive notice of the fact itself under Civ. Code § 19` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a person has constructive notice of the fact itself under Civ. Code § 19` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Gov. Code § 18, § 9612: State, and the military service terms`

#ASSERT `the meaning of State in the Government Code` FALSE EQUALS `the State of California`
#ASSERT `the meaning of State in the Government Code` TRUE EQUALS `the part of the United States, including the District of Columbia and the territories`
#ASSERT `a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `United States Army` `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `United States Army` `given that` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `Army of the United States` `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `Army of the United States` `given that` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `United States Navy` `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `United States Navy` `given that` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `military service` `given that` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `military service` `given that` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `another term` `given that` FALSE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9612 names four terms; it does not say whether any other term includes the United States Air Force"
#ASSERT REFUSED `a term in a statute is deemed to include the United States Air Force` `another term` `given that` TRUE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9612 names four terms; it does not say whether any other term includes the United States Air Force"
